Relay the engine's `info string CHAT:` lines into lichess game chat.

SquareFish narrates its own decisions (scripts/squarefish/chat.mts). A UCI
engine has no way to reach lichess chat, so the bridge has to carry it: the
engine emits `info string CHAT:<text>` alongside its bestmove and this forwards
it after the move is played.

Sent to BOTH rooms. The original lived only on the server and sent to "player",
so anyone watching saw a silent bot (#149) — the spectator is the one who most
benefits, having no other reason to know what this account is.

Failures are swallowed on purpose: chat is a garnish, and lichess rate-limits
it. A bot that stops playing because it could not say something is worse than a
quiet bot.

Applies to lichess-bot @ 2026.7.11.2. `git apply --check` first; if it fails,
the bridge has moved and the hook needs re-siting rather than forcing.

